Orbiton (invoked as o) is a small, self-contained, configuration-free
VT100 terminal text editor and lightweight IDE designed for rapid
edit-format-compile-run cycles without configuration files or plugins.

Features and behavior:
* Instant syntax highlighting across dozens of programming, markup, and
  configuration languages, with rainbow parentheses and smart indentation.
* Single-keystroke code formatting (ctrl-w) and building/running (ctrl-b)
  for C, C++, Go, Rust, Zig, Python, Shell, Odin, Haskell, and more,
  plus headless CLI modes (o --fmt and o --build).
* Basic GDB, LLDB, and Delve debugger integration, simple LSP tab
  completion, definition/include jumping, and macro recording.
* Multi-line block and function copy-paste, cross-file "portals", simple
  Markdown table editing, HTML/PDF export, and basic built-in
  spellchecking.
* Built-in man page viewer (MANPAGER=o), 16-color terminal image preview,
  file browser, /etc/fstab formatter, and optional Pico/Nano mode (-a).
* Saves and quits immediately without confirmation prompts.
* Automatically strips trailing whitespace and converts CRLF line endings
  to LF when possible.
* Requires /dev/tty for interactive editing (not needed for headless modes
  such as --fmt and --build).
